-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $EF=FE={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $FG=GF={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $F={G}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $EF=FE={I}_{3}.$ Computing $EF$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $FE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FE & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $FG=GF={I}_{3}.$ Computing $FG$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FG & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $F\\ne {G}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e493eb59-09aa-532b-acaf-dcd3967c268c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451549} {:answer/id #uuid "5eabfd91-4aa6-583d-b86d-836095be241a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451550} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a2e580-f385-518a-bca2-50adf41ac690" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e8dfef5-800b-5f06-a7b3-cca50500ee1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451551} {:answer/id #uuid "1766099c-21d2-5f82-a7a3-13809129d3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451551} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae44e41-c376-5d7d-800c-6a09f7ac5681" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8cb60d2-65e5-5ba3-bf45-7d7ea083f7b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451553} {:answer/id #uuid "9db9c520-b4ce-5fbb-ac56-6d7ad70511e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451554} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed442b50-7aef-5f8f-92c4-b56ec6bb8d50" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452624}] :question/id #uuid "f92abf10-8722-55a7-bc74-caa2837edd9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71876" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CD=DC={I}_{3}$\n\n- **II.** $CE=EC={I}_{3}$\n\n- **III.** $D={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $CE=EC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CE & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f54242e1-7020-5a41-a926-bafc9fc2bfaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451555} {:answer/id #uuid "eceddc36-fb4c-5de8-9c2a-5188fd8d48c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451555} :answer-field/id #uuid "98305e3a-4f27-53e0-84d9-532aec2ca50f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6c11d0-5258-